
"smart_sources:Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/nations/Nations - Kingdom of Duran.md": {"path":"Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/nations/Nations - Kingdom of Duran.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"rhh1cd","at":1777331817895},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1777071370729,"size":3705,"at":1777331817922,"hash":"rhh1cd"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,44],"#Nations - Kingdom of Duran":[46,47],"#Duran is Flora’s primary rival to the east, a kingdom defined by its resilience, artistry, and traditional culture.":[48,57],"#Duran is Flora’s primary rival to the east, a kingdom defined by its resilience, artistry, and traditional culture.#{1}":[49,57]},"outlinks":[],"metadata":{"type":"lore","status":"active","priority":120,"tags":["#lorebook"],"keys":["duran","duranian","bonnie prince charlie","loth logan","nisra","iris","maya"],"refine_keys":["prince charlie","cold war","estra","loren","war","duranian politics","iris","maya"],"position":"after","depth":4,"scanDepth":"1\n**What is this?** The Kingdom of Duran is a traditional, artisan-focused monarchy and Flora’s primary rival to the east. Defined by resilience, misty geography, and a culture of craftsmanship, it is the player’s homeland.\n**When to select this entry:** - Setting involves diplomatic, military, or economic interactions between Duran and Flora. - Story focuses on the player’s royal lineage, abduction backstory, or the royal family. - Scenes set in misty, mountainous, or village-focused regions. - Characters reference national grief, elite military doctrine, or trade in luxury goods.\n**Key relationships:** - **Flora** – primary rival (abductor of the player). - **King & Queen Consort Maya** – aging monarchs, player’s parents. - **Crown Prince Charlie** – regent, charismatic twin brother. - **Princess Iris** – fraternal twin sister, player’s sibling. - **{{user}}** – the “lost prince,” abducted by Flora as a child, central to national grief.","summary":"**Duran** is a traditional, mist-covered kingdom east of Flora, defined by resilience, craftsmanship, and a strong monarchy. **Select this entry** when the story involves Duran’s geography, culture, political dynamics, economy, or military doctrine—especially regarding its rivalry with Flora, the royal family, or the abduction of the \"lost prince\" ({{user}}).\n\n**Key Relationships:**\n- **Flora:** Duran’s primary rival; the source of national grief over {{user}}’s abduction.\n- **Royal Family:** Aging King, Queen Consort Maya, Crown Prince Charlie (regent), Princess Iris (fraternal twin), and the \"lost prince\" {{user}}.\n- **Economy:** Trade-dependent; imports raw materials, exports artisanal goods (jewelry, clocks, fine clothing).\n- **Military:** Elite, quality-focused; famous archers; morale boosted by artistic armor."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/nations/Nations - Kingdom of Duran.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"hs6gva","at":1777331817895},"key":"Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/nations/Nations - Kingdom of Duran.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,44],"size":2164,"outlinks":[],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
